What is an Error?

An Error is a serious problem that occurs in a program. Errors can happen during compile time or runtime.

Definition

An error is a problem that prevents a program from compiling or running correctly.

Types of Errors
=>Compile-time Error
Found by the compiler before the program runs.
Example: Missing semicolon, incorrect syntax.
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {

        System.out.println("Hello")   // Missing ;

    }
}

Output

';' expected
=>Runtime Error (Exception)
Happens while the program is running.
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {

        int a = 10;
        int b = 0;

        System.out.println(a / b);

    }
}

Output
Exception in thread "main"
java.lang.ArithmeticException: / by zero
 

What is Exception?
Exception is an unexpected event or error that occurs while a program is running (runtime) and interrupts the normal flow of the program
Why is Exception Handling Used?

Exception handling is used to:

Prevent the program from crashing.
Handle runtime errors gracefully.
Display meaningful error messages.
Allow the program to continue executing after an error.
Improve the reliability and stability of the program.
two types exception
 =>checked 
=>unchecked

Checked Exception
Definition

A Checked Exception is an exception that is checked by the compiler at compile time.

The programmer must handle the exception using try-catch or throws. Otherwise, the program will not compile.

Common Examples
IOException
FileNotFoundException
SQLException

example (Without Handling)
import java.io.FileReader;

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {

        FileReader file = new FileReader("data.txt");

    }
}
Output
Compile-time Error

Unhandled exception type FileNotFoundException

Solution Using try-catch
import java.io.FileReader;

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        try {
            FileReader file = new FileReader("data.txt");
            System.out.println("File Opened Successfully.");
        } catch (FileNotFoundException e) {
            System.out.println("File Not Found.");
        }
    }
}
Output (If file does not exist)
File Not Found.

SQLException
Definition

SQLException occurs when an error happens while working with a database, such as connecting to the database or executing an SQL query.

Example (Without Handling)
import java.sql.Connection;
import java.sql.DriverManager;
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {

        Connection con = DriverManager.getConnection(
            "jdbc:mysql://localhost:3306/test",
            "root",
            "1234"
        );

    }
}
Output
Compile-time Error

Unhandled exception type SQLException
Reason
The database may not be running.
The username or password may be incorrect.
The connection may fail.
Therefore, Java forces you to handle this checked exception.
Solution
import java.sql.Connection;
import java.sql.DriverManager;
import java.sql.SQLException;
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        try {
            Connection con = DriverManager.getConnection(
                "jdbc:mysql://localhost:3306/test",
                "root",
                "1234"
            );
            System.out.println("Database Connected.");
        } catch (SQLException e) {
            System.out.println("Database Connection Failed.");

        }

    }
}
Output (If connection fails)
Database Connection Failed.

unchecked exception
An unchecked exception is an exception that is not checked by the compiler. It occurs during runtime, and although handling it is optional, it is recommended to prevent the program from crashing.
types
ArithmeticException
NullPointerException
ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException
NumberFormatException
InputMismatchException

Example Without Exception Handling
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int a = 10;
        int b = 0;
        System.out.println(a / b);
        System.out.println("Program End");
    }
}
Output
Exception in thread "main" java.lang.ArithmeticException: / by zero
The program tries to divide 10 by 0.
Java throws an ArithmeticException.
The program stops immediately.
"Program End" is not printed.
Example With Exception Handling
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        try {
            int a = 10;
            int b = 0;
            System.out.println(a / b);
        } catch (ArithmeticException e) {
            System.out.println("Cannot divide by zero.");
        }
        System.out.println("Program End");
    }
}
Output
Cannot divide by zero.
Program End
