File Handling
File Handling is used to perform operations such as create, read, write, and delete files stored on the computer
Why is File Handling Used?

We use File Handling to:

=> Store data permanently.
=> Read data from a file.
=>Write data to a file.
=> Update file contents.
=>Delete unwanted files.

  File             Create, delete, and 
             check files

FileWriter	Write data into a file
FileReader	Read data from a file
BufferedReader	Read file line by line
Scanner	       Read data from a file

File Handling Methods
Method	Purpose
createNewFile()	 Creates a new file
exists()	Checks whether the file exists
delete()	Deletes the file
write()	          Writes data into the file
close()        	Closes the file
hasNextLine()	Checks whether another line exists
nextLine()	Reads one line from the file

Create a File
createNewFile() is used to create a new file.
If the file is created successfully, it returns true.
If the file already exists, it returns false.
Syntax
File file = new File("filename.txt");
file.createNewFile();

Program
import java.io.File;
import java.io.IOException;

public class Main {

    public static void main(String[] args) {

        try {

            File file = new File("student.txt");

            if (file.createNewFile()) {

                System.out.println("File Created Successfully.");

            } else {

                System.out.println("File Already Exists.");

            }

        } catch (IOException e) {

            System.out.println("Error Creating File.");

        }

    }

}
Output (First Time)
File Created Successfully.
Output (If File Already Exists)
File Already Exists.
